WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.680
The Conjuring 3 is chock full of easter eggs
from secret Annabelle and Nun connections

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.970
to classic horror movie tributes and clues
to the movie's big twists and reveals.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:14.180
Yippee ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing all the things you

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.079
might have missed in The Devil Made Me Do
It and explaining how the movie connects to

00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:20.269
the wider Conjuring universe.

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:22.630
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:27.230
The creepy Annabelle doll is an iconic figure
in the Conjuring franchise and The Devil Made

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.630
Me Do It expands on the story behind the satanic
cult "Disciples of the Ram" from the first

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:36.460
Annabelle movie, where one of the its members,
Annabelle Higgins, murdered her adoptive parents,

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.350
before going on to attack Mia and John Form.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:44.850
In the Conjuring 3, Ed and Lorraine meet Father
Kastner, a priest who investigated and exposed

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.370
"The Disciples of the Ram".

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:51.219
Kastner tells the Warrens they shouldn't underestimate
the power of these Satanists, and when Ed

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:54.359
asks him why someone would target an innocent
child...

00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:55.359
"The "why" is irrelevant.

00:00:55.359 --> 00:00:59.980
The "why" is counter to everything that the
Satanist stands for.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.170
His sole aim is chaos."

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:06.160
...echoes what Detective Clarkin told the
Forms in Annabelle about what he'd learned

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.160
about the cult.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.980
"That they did this to prove their devotion.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.360
A sort of violence for violence's sake."

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.930
While researching the Disciples of the Ram,
Kastner collected various occult objects and

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:20.690
books, and kept them locked in his basement
room, similar to the Warrens' artefact room

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:24.990
where they keep the Annabelle doll and many
cursed and haunted objects from their investigations.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:28.880
And his answer to Lorraine's suggestion that
he should burn all of it...

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:29.880
"I've thought of it.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.430
But I felt it was safer to keep them locked.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.530
I like taking guns off the streets."

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:39.270
...is similar to what Ed said in The Conjuring
when we were first introduced to the Warrens'

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.270
Artefact room.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.870
"Why not just throw them in an incinerator?"

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.640
"Well, that would only destroy the vessel.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.310
Sometimes it's better to keep the genie in
the bottle.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.250
It's kind of like keeping guns off the street."

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.080
And there's another Conjuring easter egg in
The Devil Made Me Do It as the Perrons, the

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.970
family from the first movie's haunted house,
are name-dropped when the Warrens receive

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:56.430
some Get Well Soon flowers.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.320
"Look what the Perron family sent.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.910
Oh, that was sweet of them."

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:04.640
The demon nun Valak was the main antagonist
in The Conjuring 2 and although she didn't

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.539
make a direct appearance in the The Devil
Made Me Do It, after Arne's been possessed

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:13.390
there's a creepy little Nun figurine in his
bedroom at the boarding kennels.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:17.811
Also in the movie's epilogue scenes is the
painting of the nun that came alive in the

00:02:17.811 --> 00:02:23.210
second Conjuring movie and which has now been
moved into the Artefact room for safekeeping.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:28.100
However, notice how the painting is kept framed
in the shot as Ed brings the Occultist's cursed

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.640
chalice into the room,
reminding us that Valak is still the principal

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.710
villain of the franchise and lurking in the
background,

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:39.620
just like Annabelle who is also carefully
framed in shot when the camera switches angles.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:43.250
By the way, there was also another little
nod to The Conjuring 2, when Lorraine sees

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.740
an upside down cross while searching for the
Occultist's location, referencing the chilling

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:51.720
scene where Janet sees all the crosses in
a room slowly turn upside down.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:56.321
A similar moment happens in the opening of
The Nun where a crucifix slowly inverts as

00:02:56.321 --> 00:03:01.010
Valak emerges from the depths of the abbey,
and in the Conjuring Universe inverted crosses

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.110
are an demonic indicator, such as the one
that appears on Frenchie's neck in the Nun

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:08.569
and which the Warrens talk about during their
presentation about possession.

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:12.850
"And like that, an upside-down cross started
to appear from within his body."

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:18.330
Valak, of course, got her own evil backstory
in The Nun movie, and a connection with The

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:22.900
Conjuring 3 that you might not have noticed
is that one of the Occultist's victims, Jessica,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.810
is played by actress Ingrid Bisu, who also
starred as Sister Oana in the demon nun's

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.070
origin story.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:33.500
The fact these two characters are played by
the same actor could throw up some interesting

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:39.220
theories about the Conjuring Universe, especially
given that spoiler alert for the Nun, Sister

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.220
Oana was already dead in that movie.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:46.810
Just before Arne murders Bruno, take a closer
look at the two posters on the wall behind

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:47.810
his landlord.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:52.250
First of all, there's Black Sabbath's iconic
album cover featuring a mysterious – even

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.709
maybe witch-like – woman, a reference to
the Occultist who is manipulating Arne in

00:03:56.709 --> 00:04:00.160
this very moment;
and then there's Ella Fitzgerald's Mack The

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:04.920
Knife, the famous song about a legendary criminal,
which foreshadows how Arne is about to pick

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.720
up a knife and become a notorious killer.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:12.050
There are a number of books you can see behind
Ed and Lorraine in the office of Arne's defence

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:16.850
attorney, but one of particular relevance
is "Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr Norrell" by Susanna

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:19.799
Clarke,
because the novel is set in an alternate history

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:25.199
of 19th-century England, much like how the
third Conjuring movie puts its own fictionalised

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:30.030
spin on real-life events, giving us an alternate
history of the Trial of Arne Johnson.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:35.650
In The Conjuring 3, director Michael Chaves
wanted to pay homage to several iconic horror

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:36.650
movies.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.809
So at the beginning of the film when Father
Gordon arrives in a cab at the Glatzel family

00:04:40.809 --> 00:04:45.559
home, with a hat, coat and briefcase, the
mist and black silhouette figure that he forms

00:04:45.559 --> 00:04:49.520
is a homage to the scene where Father Merrin
arrives in The Exorcist.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.409
Other references to the iconic film include
how David wears speckled blue pyjamas during

00:04:54.409 --> 00:04:56.400
the exorcism like Regan.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.030
And how Arne sacrifices himself for David
by inviting the demon into his body, similar

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:05.770
to Father Karras in the The Exorcist, although
the outcome, of course, is different.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:10.370
Chaves also says that the figure of Arne appearing
in a window as Father Gordon arrives is a

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:14.699
deliberate reference to Janet Leigh "seeing
Mother in the window" when she first arrives

00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:16.689
at the Bates Motel in Psycho.

00:05:16.689 --> 00:05:21.509
And the shot of David being showered with
blood inside the bathtub may also be a nod

00:05:21.509 --> 00:05:24.699
to the iconic shower scene in that same film.

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:28.800
The waterbed scene in The Devil Made Me Do
It is also another deliberate tribute by the

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.300
director to one of the first horror movies
he ever saw, "A Nightmare on Elm Street 4:

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.660
The Dream Master".

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:39.199
So when David senses a face appearing to him
from inside the mattress, it's similar to

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:43.719
how Joey in Elm Street 4 sees a model appear
to him inside the bed.

00:05:43.719 --> 00:05:48.110
And the hand bursting out of the mattress
to grab David is a nod to how Freddy Krueger

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.710
jumps out of the waterbed to attack Joey.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:55.180
When Ed is possessed by the Occultist while
he's searching for Lorraine in the tunnels,

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:59.639
the shots of him holding a hammer and dragging
his injured leg along are a little hat-tip

00:05:59.639 --> 00:06:03.900
to the showdown at the end of The Shining
where Jack Torrance limps along with an axe,

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.009
and is, like Ed, being influenced by an evil
entity.

00:06:07.009 --> 00:06:12.219
There's an Annabelle easter egg via the name
of the Palmeri Funeral Home which Ed and Lorraine

00:06:12.219 --> 00:06:16.830
visit to try and make a connection with the
Occultist through Jessica's dead body.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:20.920
Palmeri was the name of the Pasadena apartment
complex that Mia and John moved to in the

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:21.920
first Annabelle.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.789
"You're the new tenants at the Palmeri."

00:06:23.789 --> 00:06:28.319
It's also the surname of Mary Ellen's crush
in Annabelle Comes Home, Bob Palmeri.

00:06:28.319 --> 00:06:29.319
"Bob's-Got-Balls.

00:06:29.319 --> 00:06:30.319
How you doing?"

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:34.650
There's also a visual shout out to Annabelle
Comes Home via the creepy colour wheel that

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:37.080
has been added to the Warrens' artefact room.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.949
The wheel terrorised Judy Warren in that movie
when it manifested the many forms Annabelle

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:43.610
has taken in the Conjuring franchise.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.650
"I like your dolls."

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:50.830
Although I prefer previous Conjuring villains
like Valak and Bathsheba, the Occultist has

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:54.990
some interesting paranormal powers such as
the ability to manipulate her victims from

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:59.720
afar and create optical illusions to trick
them into acts they wouldn't do.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:04.629
She made Arne Johnson think his landlord was
some kind of hellish creature attacking him,

00:07:04.629 --> 00:07:09.259
and also made Ed Warren momentarily think
Lorraine was an evil monster.

00:07:09.259 --> 00:07:14.639
The Occultist had a copy of Lorraine appear
in front of her, mirroring her movements exactly.

00:07:14.639 --> 00:07:19.009
This trippy moment was foreshadowed at the
beginning of the movie during David's exorcism

00:07:19.009 --> 00:07:21.949
when the camera that Drew was filming with
was knocked over.

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:26.690
As the camera continued to film, it was pointed
towards a TV that was screening the live recording,

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:30.719
causing an image of the screen to replicate
itself endlessly.

00:07:30.719 --> 00:07:34.860
This was a neat visual piece of foreshadowing
that was originally going to lead in to an

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:38.279
even more trippy sequence than we got in the
final movie.

00:07:38.279 --> 00:07:42.349
In the trailers for the movie, you can see
a deleted scene where Lorraine sees many copies

00:07:42.349 --> 00:07:47.069
of herself, replicating endlessly in a spiral
of sorts into the distance.

00:07:47.069 --> 00:07:51.469
And if you want to learn more about that and
all the other deleted scenes including a cut

00:07:51.469 --> 00:07:55.369
post-credits scene, I'll be talking about
all that in my next Conjuring video.

00:07:55.369 --> 00:07:59.930
I'll add a link for you to watch it here and
in the video description as soon as it's ready.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.650
So what did you think of the The Devil Made
Me Do It?

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:05.809
And how does it compare to your other favourite
movies in this franchise?

00:08:05.809 --> 00:08:08.289
Let me know in the comments below.

00:08:08.289 --> 00:08:12.979
If you enjoyed this, leave a thumbs-up;
and a share is also hugely appreciated.

